when the screen is resized, the info boxes aren't repositioned correctly. They
should be anchored to the viewport, not the world.

if the user moves the mouse back-and-forth rapidly, it's possible to spawn many
balls at once. We should add a cooldown that is intended to be modified later
on, when we implement future features like upgrades and such. If the user is
unable to spawn a ball because there is another ball inside the spawn radius,
then instead of wasting that opportunity we should think of a way to "save" that
extra spawn time, so the user isn't rewarded for flicking the mouse back and
forth, and they aren't penalized for leaving it alone. This should also have the
benefit of "standardizing" the output of balls per second, even if they are
unable to spawn immediately, they should still spawn at roughly the same rate.
